### Did Dr. Anthony Fauci ever state or write the phrase "I can’t imagine that … anybody could be doing more" in reference to Donald Trump's COVID-19 pandemic response?
Answer: Yes, Dr. Anthony Fauci did state the phrase "I can't imagine that under any circumstances that anybody could be doing more," but he was speaking about the dedication of himself and other members of the White House Coronavirus Task Force, not specifically praising Donald Trump's personal efforts. In a March 2020 interview on Fox News' "Life, Liberty & Levin," Fauci said, "I'm down at the White House virtually every day with the Task Force... I'm not the only one. There's a whole group of us that are doing that... So I can't imagine that under any circumstances that anybody could be doing more." As the source clarifies, "Fauci does not mention Trump specifically at any point leading up to the quote, and appears to reference the hours being put in by himself and other Task Force members."

